1. Project objective

PhishGuard began as a hackathon solution for detecting phishing emails and
malicious attachments. The intended product combined:

live Gmail ingestion;

email-header and content analysis;

machine-learning phishing classification;

attachment risk identification;

a combined explainable risk score;

DFIR-style reports and recommended actions; and

future integration with YARA, threat intelligence and a sandbox.

The project was deliberately implemented as a safe prototype. It reads email
through Gmail's API, but it does not visit URLs, execute attachments or detonate
malware.

