3. Stage-by-stage development history

Stage 1 — Problem definition and functional design

The original scope separated the tool into two principal scanners.

Email scanner

The proposed indicators included:

fake or impersonated senders;

email-header inconsistencies;

sender IP and routing information;

metadata extraction;

typosquatting and lookalike domains;

urgency and social-engineering language;

credential, OTP and personal-data requests;

URL analysis;

sender-authentication results; and

an overall trust or risk score.

Attachment scanner

The proposed checks included:

extension and file-type validation;

double-extension detection;

hashes and reputation;

YARA classification;

Trojan, worm, ransomware, RAT, APT, botnet and fileless indicators; and

eventual isolated sandbox execution.

The first interface design used five modules:

Inbox

Email Analysis

Malware Analyser

Risk Assessment

Reports

At this stage the interface used controlled demonstration data. Gmail OAuth,
live message retrieval and real sandboxing were not yet connected.

