5. Current end-to-end operating workflow

Application startup

Backend terminal:

cd backend
venv\Scripts\activate
uvicorn api:app --reload --port 8000

Frontend terminal:

cd frontend
npm run dev

Inbox workflow

The frontend calls GET /api/messages.

The backend obtains every Gmail Inbox page.

It retrieves display metadata for each message.

SQLite adds saved scan state where available.

The frontend displays saved verdicts or Pending.

Analysis workflow

The user selects a message.

The frontend calls the message-analysis endpoint.

The backend returns a cached result unless a forced rerun was requested.

A fresh scan retrieves the complete Gmail message.

MIME text, HTML, headers and attachment names are extracted.

The 12 rules and one ML classifier run.

Points are combined and capped at 100.

A verdict, severity, evidence and recommendations are returned.

The result is stored in SQLite.

The frontend animates and displays the evidence.

Offline MBOX workflow

The raw corpus stays offline.

analyze_mbox.py adapts each message into the same internal format.

The same detection engine runs without Gmail.

CSV and JSONL evidence files are produced for batch review.

